  "name": "Mak yong (Malay dance-drama)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Malay dance-drama of Kelantan, the Patani region and the Riau Islands, proclaimed by UNESCO a Masterpiece of the Oral and Intangible Heritage of Humanity and later inscribed on its Representative List; it combines acting, dance, song and improvised dialogue, and the leading prince role (Pak Yong) is played by a woman. Performances open by saluting the rebab, the three-string spike fiddle that leads the ensemble of a pair of gendang barrel drums, a pair of hanging tetawak gongs and, in some pieces, serunai shawm, canang kettle gongs and kesi cymbals.",
